@voice halloran-emeka
// Works writer. Emeka Halloran (he/him): Works systems officer, day shift, cabin 4-13. Kind, loyal. Swapped his days
// off with Torres (now Sat-Sun) so Torres can meet you. Tea break, garden lover, late sleeper. Tells terrible jokes
// at breakfast (the worst on the ship; he trades them with Yoon, Lemaire and Yilmaz). Bakes on rest days, one oven
// at a time, when Brennan allows it. Gives you the new hand's mug at Works Friday tea on Day 5.
//
// HOW HE TALKS: warm and unhurried; laughs at his own joke before he reaches the end of it. "Lovely" a lot. Always
// asks if you've eaten. Long, friendly sentences that wander a bit.
// WITH JUNIORS: a big brother. Covers for small mistakes, then quietly shows you how.
// WHAT HE NOTICES: who looks tired, who's skipped a meal, whose turn it is on the tea rota.
// MOOD TELLS: low = no joke at breakfast, and people notice; high = two jokes, both worse.
// NEVER: says no to anyone (that's his thread); unkind jokes (his are terrible, never mean).
// RUNNING: the breakfast joke; Brennan's oven ("her kingdom; I need a visa"); the mug rack at the tea corner.
tpl: warm
talk: Warm and unhurried; laughs before the punchline; says "lovely" a lot; always asks if you've eaten.
cares: the Works team looked after | baking, when Brennan lets him near an oven | the Friday tea rota | the garden's tomatoes
jokes: one terrible joke every breakfast, and nobody can stop him | Brennan's oven is a kingdom and he needs a visa | the mug rack at the tea corner, which he keeps
hi: Morning, morning | Hello, you | Ah, hello
bye: Look after yourself | Off you pop | Ta-ta for now
yes: Course I will | Lovely, yes | Happy to
thanks: Ah, lovely | You're a treasure | Thanks ever so
wow: Ooh, look at that | Well, isn't that grand
sigh: Oh, dear me | Ah, well
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: practical
openness: open
loves: sweet | made
likes: tea | garden
invites: works-tea | garden
joy: baking, and the face people make at a warm scone
keepsake: a scone tin with a dent in the lid
avoid: saying no (it's his thread) | jokes about anyone but himself
